---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageHeader from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/PageHeader.astro";
import Print from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/Print.astro";
import { sources } from "../lib/site.mjs";

sources("devices", [
  "The owner's statement of 2026-11-18: the Pixel 10a is the daily phone, the Pixel 7a the development phone (decision 256).",
  "docs/devices/support-policy.md (the entry gate for a supported device)",
  "The images paragraph is the owner's intention of 2026-11-18, recorded as decision 256.",
  "What works on each phone is not on this page until the owner states it.",
]);
---
<Page
  title="Devices: ObliviOS"
  description="Which phones run ObliviOS today: the Pixel 10a I use every day and the Pixel 7a I develop on. No device is supported yet, and what has to be true before one is."
  path="/devices"
  current="/devices"
>
  <PageHeader crumb="Devices" title="Devices" lede="Which phones run ObliviOS, which one I use every day, and what has to be true before I call any of them supported.">
    <Print id="ph" label="Two phones, one large and one small" />
  </PageHeader>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c lead">
      <div>
        <p class="big">No device is supported. Two phones run ObliviOS builds: the Pixel 10a I use every day, and the Pixel 7a I develop on.</p>
        <p class="fn">ObliviOS is source only: there is no image to flash.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="c gap-top">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Pixel 10a <code>stallion</code></dt>
        <dd>My daily phone.</dd>
        <dt>Pixel 7a <code>lynx</code></dt>
        <dd>My development phone.</dd>
        <dt>Supported</dt>
        <dd>No device. A device counts as supported only after it passes the entry gate below.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What supported means</h2>
        <p>A device is supported only with verified upstream device source, current firmware and driver coverage, a monthly update path, signed images and updates, locked-bootloader verification, recovery validation, and evidence for emergency and radio functions. A booting image alone is not support, and a phone that I use myself is not a support claim.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Images</h2>
        <p>If real interest in ObliviOS shows, I want to publish images for the Pixel 10a. I have not set a date. Before I do, the five gates of a public beta on the <a href="/status">status page</a> have to be met, and I decide on the day, separately. Until then ObliviOS is source only.</p>
        <div class="callout"><h3>No date, no promise</h3><p>Nothing on this page says that an image will exist. It says what I intend and what stands in the way.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
